== 1. the reader ==
  ok    a declaration reads as shape / name / text
  ok    'none — reason' reads as the explicit no-control declaration
  ok    a header with no MUST-FIRE line declares nothing
== 1b. the header is the leading comment block (R30): a bare # does not end it, the first code line does ==
  ok    a declaration after a bare # line is read (bbh: 264 of 315 gates have one within five lines)
CONTROL FIRED: body-is-not-header — a MUST-FIRE line after the first code line declares nothing (its firing will read as undeclared)
== 2. the runner's controls block, one gate at a time ==
  ok    g_ok -> OK, runner exit 0
  ok    g_none -> OK, runner exit 0
  ok    g_undecl -> RED, runner exit 1
  ok    g_deadline -> RED, runner exit 1
  ok    g_silent -> UNDECLARED, runner exit 1
== 3. MUST-FIRE: a declared control that never fires ==
CONTROL FIRED: dead-control — g_dead (declared, never fired) made the runner NOT GREEN, exit 1
  ok    a dead control refuses the verdict (BBX-6)
== 4. without enforcement the block is absent and the output is bbh's ==
  ok    enforce = false: no controls block, GREEN (fidelity with bbh)

PASS: declared controls are read, dead ones refuse the verdict, silence is red under enforcement
